<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28465" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕles</span></b> , ētis,
			m., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μέλης</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a river in Ionia, near
				Smyrna, on the banks of which, it is said, Homer was born</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				5, 29, 31, § 118</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Stat. S. 2,
				7, 33</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 3, 60</span></i>.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕlētēus</span></b> , a,
			um, <i>adj., Meletean</i>, <b>poet.</b> for <i>Homeric</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">chartae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tib.
					4, 1, 200</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕ-lētīnus</span></b> , a,
			um, <i>adj., Meletine</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">deae,</span>”
				<i>dwelling at Meles</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					4, 236</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
